WEBVTT

00:03.600 --> 00:06.830
Try your mobile app on a real phone
in seconds.

00:06.880 --> 00:10.580
This is the Expo Go preview
in WaveMaker Studio.

00:11.530 --> 00:13.290
Preview your React Native app,

00:13.340 --> 00:16.300
then open the QR panel
from the toolbar.

00:17.210 --> 00:19.050
First, install Expo Go.

00:19.100 --> 00:22.780
Use the version that matches
your project's Expo SDK,

00:22.830 --> 00:24.570
shown right in the panel.

00:25.500 --> 00:27.640
Pick Android or iOS,

00:27.690 --> 00:31.910
then scan the code, or paste
the Expo link into Expo Go.

00:31.960 --> 00:34.040
Your app opens right away.

00:34.970 --> 00:39.190
Now you can try touch gestures and
native features on a real phone,

00:39.240 --> 00:40.910
without building an app.

00:41.830 --> 00:45.250
Change something in Studio,
and it rebuilds on its own.

00:45.300 --> 00:48.920
Just shake your phone and tap Reload
in the developer menu.

00:49.940 --> 00:53.070
The Expo Go preview
in WaveMaker Studio.

00:53.120 --> 00:56.130
Build in Studio,
feel it on your phone.
